<script>
  (() => {
    const section = document.querySelector("#blueman-complete-page .story .bp-inner");
    if (!section) return;
    const artworks = [...document.querySelectorAll("img")];
    const findArt = title => artworks.find(image => image.alt.startsWith(title));
    const lifeArt = findArt("A small word can change somebody's life");
    const peopleArt = findArt("Always choose people over money");
    const gallery = lifeArt && peopleArt ? `<div class="story-gallery"><figure class="story-print"><img src="${lifeArt.src}" alt="${lifeArt.alt}"></figure><figure class="story-print"><img src="${peopleArt.src}" alt="${peopleArt.alt}"></figure></div>` : "";
    section.innerHTML = `
      <header class="story-head"><div class="bp-kicker">How it all began</div><h2 class="bp-title">One idea.<br><span class="cyan">A story still being written.</span></h2></header>
      ${gallery}
      <div class="story-roadmap">
        <article class="story-step"><div class="story-time">Early 2018</div><i class="story-node"></i><details class="story-accordion"><summary>Communication through pictures</summary><div class="story-copy">
          <p>Our story started in early 2018 with a simple challenge I had: finding a way to express myself to others the way I see things in my mind.</p>
          <p>In the beginning, I needed those pictures mainly to help explain my thoughts and ideas during public speaking. When standing in front of an audience, I wanted people to be able to see and feel the ideas I was trying to share, not just hear the words.</p>
          <p>For me, words have not always come naturally. I often have a clear vision, thought or feeling in my mind, but finding the right words to help someone else see exactly what I see has not always been easy.</p>
          <p>The visions were clear. The pictures were already there. But turning them into words that could help others see exactly the same thing was not always possible.</p>
          <p>That is where pictures became more than just pictures.</p><p>They became my way of communicating.</p>
          <p>A way to take something that existed in my mind and make it visible to someone else. A way to share an idea, a feeling or a perspective without having to find the perfect words for it.</p>
          <p>So the search began.</p><p>Picture after picture. Search after search. Looking for images that could help express those thoughts and bring them to life.</p><p>But there was one problem.</p>
          <p>The exact pictures I needed simply did not exist.</p><p>No matter how much I searched, the pictures on the internet could never fully capture what was already clear in my mind.</p>
          <p>Eventually, I realized that finding the right picture was not enough. I needed to find someone who could understand what I saw and bring the picture in my mind to life.</p>
          <p>So I started looking for an artist. And in March 2018, I found the right person.</p>
          <p>From the very first meeting, there was an immediate understanding. Ideas could be shared, discussed and brought to life naturally. The collaboration was made even easier by the values we shared.</p>
          <p>After about a year of working together, the journey began to evolve and take on a new form.</p><p>Those pictures were no longer just a way for me to express thoughts.</p>
          <p>They began to carry thoughts, emotions and stories of their own. But there was still one thing missing.</p>
          <p>The pictures needed someone to bring them to life. Someone who could carry the ideas, emotions and stories behind them from one picture to the next. Someone who could feel, think, fail, learn, smile and experience life just like the rest of us.</p>
          <p>And that someone was BlueMan.</p>
          <h3>MORE THAN A WAY TO COMMUNICATE</h3>
          <p>What started as my way of communicating soon became something much more personal: a way of holding on to the things life had taught me.</p>
          <p>Experiences pass. Moments fade. Lessons can be forgotten. But some moments leave something behind: a realization, a feeling or a different way of seeing the world.</p>
          <p>Most of the pictures are born from those moments. From personal experiences, challenges that have been faced and lessons learned along the way.</p>
          <p>Creating pictures became a way for me to capture those moments and give them a place to stay. Instead of simply writing down what life had taught me, I could turn those experiences and lessons into something visual. Something I could return to, remember and experience again.</p>
          <p>Sometimes an experience becomes a thought. Sometimes that thought becomes a message. And sometimes, it becomes a picture.</p>
          <p>In many ways, the pictures became a visual record of my experiences, lessons and moments that life had left behind.</p>
        </div></details></article>
        <article class="story-step"><div class="story-time">March 2018</div><i class="story-node"></i><details class="story-accordion"><summary>The artist who brought the ideas to life</summary><div class="story-copy">
          <p>Behind every SuccessPictures picture is the same artist who has been there from the beginning.</p>
          <p>Before becoming part of this journey, creating art was already his passion. He loved painting on walls and bringing ideas to life, but at the time, art was not yet his full-time profession. He was also working as a chef and could only dedicate his free time to what he truly loved doing.</p>
          <p>Soon after the collaboration began, something changed.</p><p>He was able to spend 100% of his time doing what he loved most: creating.</p>
          <p>It is crazy to think that during the first year, every single picture was drawn by hand on paper and then scanned into a computer. There were no shortcuts. Just an idea, a piece of paper and the hands of an artist.</p>
          <p>In May 2019, he bought a drawing tablet, making the process a little easier. But the heart of the process has remained the same ever since.</p>
          <p>An idea is born. It is shared. And through the artist's hands, it becomes a picture.</p>
        </div></details></article>
        <article class="story-step"><div class="story-time">May 2019</div><i class="story-node"></i><details class="story-accordion"><summary>One place – SuccessPictures was born</summary><div class="story-copy">
          <p>As more pictures began to take shape, a simple question emerged:</p><p>Why keep them only to ourselves?</p>
          <p>Every picture carried a thought, a lesson, a feeling or a moment that had been captured along the way. What had started as something personal slowly began to feel like something that could be shared.</p>
          <p>Perhaps a picture that came from one person's experience could mean something to someone else. Perhaps a lesson learned along the way could help another person see something differently. Or perhaps, at the right moment, a single picture could simply make someone's day a little better.</p>
          <p>And if there was even a small chance of that, sharing them felt like the right thing to do.</p><p>So, in May 2019, SuccessPictures was born.</p>
          <p>Not simply as a place to share pictures, but as a place to share thoughts, experiences and moments that might mean something to someone else.</p>
          <p>What started with pictures created to capture life slowly became a way to give something back through them.</p>
          <p>And with every picture shared, there was a possibility that somewhere, someone might find exactly what they needed at that moment.</p>
          <p>From the very beginning, it became clear that these pictures could mean something to others too. As SuccessPictures began to grow, so did the community around it. More and more people began finding their way to the pictures every day, becoming part of a growing community built around shared thoughts, experiences and the simple belief that a picture can make a difference.</p>
        </div></details></article>
        <article class="story-step"><div class="story-time">The family</div><i class="story-node"></i><details class="story-accordion"><summary>A team of three</summary><div class="story-copy">
          <p>As the community began to grow, so did the desire to stay connected to the people who had become part of the journey.</p>
          <p>Because I have always been a total introvert and much more comfortable expressing my thoughts through pictures than through words, communicating with a growing community did not always come naturally.</p>
          <p>So a friend joined the journey.</p>
          <p>Someone who shared the same values and saw the world in a very similar way. Someone who understood what BlueMan and the pictures stood for and became a connecting link between the ideas behind them and the growing BlueMan Family.</p>
          <p>You could almost think of her as a second BlueMan. Always there to support, answer questions, stay in touch and simply care about how everyone is doing.</p>
          <p>She became the heart and soul of the BlueMan Family.</p><p>And just like that, the journey became a team of three.</p><p>Different people. Different strengths.</p><p>One shared heart.</p>
          <p>Together, we continue to create and share pictures with one simple hope: that something we create today might make someone's tomorrow a little better.</p>
        </div></details></article>
        <article class="story-step"><div class="story-time">Over the years</div><i class="story-node"></i><details class="story-accordion"><summary>More than just pictures</summary><div class="story-copy">
          <p>Over the years, we have seen something that we could never have planned in the beginning.</p><p>A picture can travel further than we ever could.</p>
          <p>It can reach someone on the other side of the world at exactly the right moment. It can make someone smile on a difficult day. It can offer a different perspective, remind someone of what truly matters or create an AHA moment that stays with them long after they scroll past it.</p>
          <p>That is what has kept us going.</p>
          <p>Not because we have all the answers, but because we believe that even a small message can make a meaningful difference when it reaches the right person at the right time.</p>
        </div></details></article>
        <article class="story-step"><div class="story-time">From day one</div><i class="story-node"></i><details class="story-accordion"><summary>People over profit</summary><div class="story-copy">
          <p>From the very beginning, we also made a conscious decision about the kind of community we wanted to build.</p><p>We chose people over profit.</p>
          <p>We never wanted the people who trusted us to feel like an audience to be monetized. We wanted SuccessPictures to remain a safe place where people know what to expect, where nothing is hidden between the lines and where trust always comes before money.</p>
          <p>That is why, since the beginning, we have never done paid promotions or changed what we create because someone was willing to pay for it.</p>
          <p>We have always created with an open heart and genuine joy, simply because we want to give something meaningful to people, without expecting anything in return.</p>
          <p>And perhaps that is the most beautiful part of this journey.</p><p>We may create the pictures, but their meaning belongs to the people who see themselves in them.</p>
        </div></details></article>
        <article class="story-step"><div class="story-time">Now</div><i class="story-node"></i><details class="story-accordion"><summary>The story continues</summary><div class="story-copy">
          <p>Looking back, it is incredible to think how one simple need to communicate in a different way could lead to all of this.</p>
          <p>One thought led to an idea. An idea led to an artist. The artist helped bring those ideas to life. The pictures found their way to people. And those people became a community.</p>
          <p>Since then, the journey has taken us further than we could have ever imagined.</p><p>But the reason we started has never changed.</p>
          <p>We are still here to create.</p><p>To share.</p><p>To give.</p>
          <p>And to keep believing that one simple picture can create a moment that changes the way someone sees the world.</p>
          <p>This is not a story about something that was built and left behind.</p><p>This is a story that is still being written.</p>
          <p>And as long as there are ideas worth sharing, stories worth telling and people who need to be reminded that there is still something good in the world, we will keep creating. 💙</p>
        </div></details></article>
        <div class="story-end">One thought became a picture. A picture became a community.<br><span>And the story is still being written.</span></div>
      </div>`;
  })();
</script>
